            "<strong>Health</strong>, in the 1948 WHO definition, is a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease or infirmity. The definition is criticised for setting a standard nobody meets, but it does the one thing the examiner wants: it reminds you that a farmer with controlled hypertension who works, worships and feeds his family may be healthier than a man with normal blood pressure who cannot leave his room for fear. Later definitions add the idea of <strong>capacity</strong> — health as the ability to adapt and to manage one's own life in the face of the challenges one meets.",
