            "A nurse admitting a patient assesses before she plans; a nurse arriving in a zone does the same for the community. <strong>Community diagnosis</strong> is the systematic collection, analysis and interpretation of information about a community's health status, its determinants and its resources, in partnership with the community, in order to identify and prioritise its health problems and plan action. It produces a <strong>community profile</strong> (the assessment), a <strong>ranked list of problems</strong> (the diagnosis), a <strong>plan</strong> with objectives and activities, <strong>implementation</strong> through local structures and <strong>evaluation</strong> against the objectives that were set. The steps mirror the nursing process exactly, which is why students who can plan care for one patient can learn to plan for 5,000.",
